                <pb facs="0395" n="363" xml:id="pg363"/>

                <head>206. Telegram From the Commander of the Sixth Fleet (Martin) to the U.S.S.
                    America and U.S.S. Saratoga<anchor n="1" xml:id="d206-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1967-06-08T13:39:00+00:00">June 8, 1967,
                            1339Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>081339Z. USS <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> Incident.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item> IAW CINCUSNAVEUR inst P03611#SB forces attacking <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Liberty</hi> are declared hostile.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>You are authorized to use force including destruction as necessary to
                        control the situation. Do not use more force than required, do not pursue
                        any unit towards land for reprisal purposes. Purpose of counterattack is to
                        protect <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> only.<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d206-f2"/>
                    </item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Brief all pilots contents this msg.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>In addition brief pilots that Egyptian territorial limit only 12 miles and
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> right on edge. Do not fly between
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> and shoreline except as required to
                        carry out provisions para 2 above. Brief fighter cover that any attacks on
                        attack aircraft, <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> or they themselves is
                        hostile act and para two above applies.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d206-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d206-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Naval Security Group Files, Box 896, USS <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Liberty</hi> Pre-76 Inactive Files, Box 1, U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Liberty</hi>, 5750/4, Chronological Message File. Confidential; Flash. The
                    message was repeated at 1349Z from COMSIXTHFLT to CNO, CINCUSNAVEUR, and CTF 60.
                    Received in the Navy Department at 1402Z. A handwritten note on the telegram
                    states that the message was cancelled by COMSIXTHFLT 081609Z. Prior to that,
                    however, telegram 081440Z from COMSIXTHFLT to the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >America</hi> and the <hi rendition="#italic">Saratoga</hi> directed:
                    “Recall all strikes.” (Naval Historical Center, Operational Archives Branch,
                    U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Liberty</hi> Incident, Message File) Telegram
                    081645Z from COMSIXTHFLT to USCINCEUR reported that all aircraft from the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">America</hi> and the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Saratoga</hi> had been recalled and were accounted for. (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d206-f2" n="2" xml:id="d206-f2-content">
                <p> JCS telegram 7354 to UNCINCEUR, 081416Z Jun 67, reads as follows: “You are
                    authorized to use whatever force required to defend USS <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Liberty</hi> from further attacks.” (Johnson Library, National Security
                    File, NSC Histories, Middle East Crisis, Vol. 7, Appendix H) JCS telegram 7369
                    to USCINCEUR, 081529Z Jun 67, confirmed a telephone conversation from Vice Chief
                    of Naval Operations Admiral Horacio Rivero to Deputy Commander in Chief, U.S.
                    European Command General David A. Burchinal USAF, cancelling this authorization.
                    (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
